            {
                "entry_id": "b5dc6cda-dad6-3b7a-8107-cd301053e7ab",
                "word": "terp",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "fa4c714c-283b-41bc-b7aa-1fb25581587c",
                        "entry_id": "b5dc6cda-dad6-3b7a-8107-cd301053e7ab",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "terps"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "a7265f71-6059-3cda-8341-b88590ae6f5c",
                        "entry_id": "b5dc6cda-dad6-3b7a-8107-cd301053e7ab",
                        "glosses": [
                            "An interpreter (person who translates)."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "e13c5851-0a6d-47e2-a48e-67b61d374518",
                                "sense_id": "a7265f71-6059-3cda-8341-b88590ae6f5c",
                                "text": "I don't think it's at all appropriate to hire a terp to review your correspondences, reports, grammar, tone, style, etc. It is completely YOUR responsibility to perform effective written communication tasks."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "14b36a52-f74f-4765-b4c6-1e4a0697f828",
                                "sense_id": "a7265f71-6059-3cda-8341-b88590ae6f5c",
                                "text": "But for troops in the new Afghan army, there is a particular irritant: Afghan interpreters working with U.S. soldiers — called terps by troops in the field — can earn more than an Afghan army officer."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6c9da8b1-5c0b-4cf3-8f76-8f1740430b08",
                                "sense_id": "a7265f71-6059-3cda-8341-b88590ae6f5c",
                                "text": "We don't understand what he's saying, of course, but he looks like he knows what he's saying. There's a certain something that emanates from a confused patient that this fellow doesn't have. I sure wish I had more 'terps. Well, we're not going to CT him right away."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "d7f61ab3-1f37-3e80-9684-efa62b151bbe",
                        "entry_id": "b5dc6cda-dad6-3b7a-8107-cd301053e7ab",
                        "glosses": [
                            "An interpreter (program that parses and executes another program)."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "slang"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "e1cd69db-507e-4770-b1a5-6609daf7579a",
                                "sense_id": "d7f61ab3-1f37-3e80-9684-efa62b151bbe",
                                "text": "So, I'm writing a Z-Machine terp. It is not done. It's getting there. Now, I have some ideas of things I would like this terp to do, but I thought it might be a nice idea to find out if there are any features that other people on this newsgroup would like in a Z-Machine terp."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1c9372d1-4558-4894-8a29-e264d459db25",
                                "sense_id": "d7f61ab3-1f37-3e80-9684-efa62b151bbe",
                                "text": "As far as I know all the TADS terps are just ports of the original."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
